// Title: HybridConnectionManager Service Installation - Registry
// Sigma ID: ac8866c7-ce44-46fd-8c17-b24acff96ca8
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2021-04-12 | Modified: 2022-11-27
// ATT&CK: resource-development, T1608
// Description: Detects the installation of the Azure Hybrid Connection Manager service to allow remote code
//   execution from Azure function.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/Cyb3rWard0g/status/1381642789369286662
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_hybridconnectionmgr_svc_installation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Services\\HybridConnectionManager" or (ActionType =~ "RegistryValueSet" and RegistryValueData contains "Microsoft.HybridConnectionManager.Listener.exe")
